<section class="method-flow" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="method-flow__inner">
    <header class="method-flow__header">
      <p class="method-flow__overline">The method</p>
      <h2 id="method-title">People provide the knowledge. AI accelerates the modelling.</h2>
      <p>
        People bring source material and domain judgement. We use AI to turn that evidence
        into a candidate model and ontology that working-group members can challenge and
        improve. Each round of feedback starts another modelling pass. Once the group reaches
        consensus, the agreed model becomes a draft standard.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="method-flow__figure" aria-labelledby="method-title method-caption">
      <div class="method-flow__composition">
        <div class="method-flow__loop">
          <img
            class="method-flow__graphic method-flow__graphic--light"
            src="/images/home/method-loop-light.svg"
            width="1085"
            height="601"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <img
            class="method-flow__graphic method-flow__graphic--dark"
            src="/images/home/method-loop-dark.svg"
            width="1085"
            height="601"
            alt=""
            aria-hidden="true"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <p class="method-flow__loop-label">
            <strong>Feedback starts the next pass.</strong>
            <span>Repeat until consensus.</span>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="method-flow__exit">
          <span class="method-flow__exit-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <article class="method-flow__outcome">
            <p>Consensus reached</p>
            <h3>The agreed model becomes a draft standard.</h3>
            <span>
              This is a stable, reviewed working-group draft. It is not yet ratified or
              adopted.
            </span>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ol class="method-flow__text-version">
        <li>People provide source material that their organisations are authorised to share.</li>
        <li>AI extracts a candidate model and ontology from that evidence.</li>
        <li>OPDA publishes the candidate with its sources, changes and open questions.</li>
        <li>Working-group members discuss, challenge and improve the candidate.</li>
        <li>Feedback and new evidence start the next AI-assisted modelling pass.</li>
        <li>When the group reaches consensus, the agreed model becomes a draft standard.</li>
      </ol>

      <figcaption id="method-caption">
        <strong>AI accelerates the work; people remain in control.</strong>
        AI can extract, compare and draft. People decide what is true, resolve disagreement
        and approve every change in status.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

